{% comment %}
  sections/featured-blog.liquid

  Articles from one blog, as a grid or a carousel.

  ## Two existing implementations, joined rather than copied

  The surface is `sections/main-faq.liquid`'s — colour scheme, background media,
  border, radius, margins and padding, the same setting ids feeding the same
  snippets. The carousel is `sections/featured-collection.liquid`'s, down to the
  last `carousel_*` id, so the arrows, the peek, the pagination and the custom
  colours are one implementation with one set of bugs and one place to fix them.

  Nothing here is a third copy of either.

  ## The card is blocks, not settings

  `snippets/article-card.liquid` still renders the blog index, where every card
  is the same and there is nothing to arrange. A featured row is the other case,
  so the card is `blocks/_article-card.liquid` and everything in it — the
  picture, the pills on it, the read time, the title, the excerpt, the button —
  is a nested block the merchant arranges once.

  It is rendered here rather than added by the merchant, with the same `id` on
  every pass, because a row decides how many cards it has. One id means one set
  of settings shared by all of them: a grid whose third card could be styled
  differently from the first is a grid that will be.

  `closest.article:` is what carries the article into the card *and* into every
  block nested inside it. `{% content_for 'blocks' %}` passes no parameters, so
  a nested Article title has no other way to know which article it is titling.
  `sections/main-product.liquid` passes `closest.product` into its detail blocks
  for exactly the same reason.

  ## Why the carousel element is written out here

  `snippets/carousel-shell.liquid` takes its slides as a captured string, and
  `content_for` output cannot be captured — Shopify renders blocks with their
  editor bindings attached, and buffering that into a variable is not something
  the platform supports. So the element and its track are written here, while
  `carousel-shell-attrs` and `carousel-shell-tail` supply the attributes and the
  controls from the same sub-snippets the shell itself uses.
  `sections/featured-collection.liquid` does the same, for the same reason.

  ## Two answers this section gives that the collection one does not

  **The empty row is drawn, not apologised for.** A blog with no posts renders
  `snippets/article-card-placeholder.liquid` across one row rather than a line
  of text. A merchant adds this section before they have written anything more
  often than after, and the theme editor is where the section is judged.

  **View all is a grid-only control.** A carousel already is the way through the
  rest of the blog, so the button is hidden — in the panel and on the page —
  whenever the desktop layout is a carousel. See the note by `show_view_all`.

  ## The settings panel is grouped by what a merchant is deciding

  Blog and count, then Layout — the two layout selects, the three column
  counts, the container and View all together, because those are one decision
  made once. Everything a carousel needs is under **Carousel**, hidden whole
  when neither breakpoint is one.

  Its colours are a select, `carousel_color_source`, rather than the
  **Use custom colors** checkbox `sections/featured-collection.liquid` still
  carries. `snippets/carousel-style.liquid` reads both, so the two sections
  share one implementation and neither had to be converted for the other.

  ### The unparenthesised `visible_if` conditions are not a typo

  A carousel setting that also depends on a toggle reads:

      carousel_navigation and layout == 'carousel' or layout_mobile == 'carousel'

  which means *navigation is on **and** either breakpoint is a carousel*.
  `visible_if` is Liquid, and Liquid has no parentheses: operators are evaluated
  right to left, so the `or` binds first and the `and` takes the whole of it.
  Writing the grouping out — `A and (B or C)` — is a `ValidVisibleIf` error,
  which is how this was found rather than guessed at.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  assign featured = s.blog
  assign limit = s.articles_to_show | default: 3 | plus: 0
  assign desktop = s.columns_desktop | default: 3 | plus: 0

  comment
    `sizes` has to describe the widest a card is ever painted, which is the
    desktop column count. Getting it wrong is the most common cause of a grid
    downloading pictures two or three times larger than it shows.
  endcomment
  assign card_width = 100 | divided_by: desktop
  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 990px) ' | append: card_width | append: 'vw, (min-width: 750px) 45vw, 90vw'

  comment
    ---- the surface, from `sections/main-faq.liquid` ----
  endcomment
  assign background_media = s.background_media | default: 'none'
  assign has_background_media = false
  if background_media != 'none'
    assign has_background_media = true
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if has_background_media == false
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | default: ''
  endif

  comment
    Opacity goes into the colour rather than onto the element: `opacity` on the
    section would fade the cards along with the frame.

    With no colour picked the border is `currentColor`, which the colour filters
    cannot take an alpha channel from — there is nothing to read until the
    scheme resolves in the browser. `color-mix` does the same fade at that point
    instead, so both paths honour the slider.
  endcomment
  assign border_width = 0
  if s.border_style == 'solid'
    assign border_width = s.border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_top = s.margin_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_bottom = s.margin_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the carousel ----

    One `matchMedia` and nothing else when both breakpoints are grids: the
    component checks before it touches Swiper, so a grid-everywhere section
    never constructs one.

    `count` is what lets `carousel-options` decide whether the merchant's Loop
    setting is achievable — Swiper silently disables looping below twice
    `slidesPerView`, which reads as the setting doing nothing.
  endcomment
  assign cs_layout = s.layout | default: 'carousel'
  assign cs_layout_mobile = s.layout_mobile | default: 'carousel'

  assign cs_count = featured.articles_count | default: 0 | plus: 0
  if cs_count > limit
    assign cs_count = limit
  endif

  assign cs_is_carousel = false
  if cs_layout == 'carousel' or cs_layout_mobile == 'carousel'
    assign cs_is_carousel = true
  endif

  comment
    ---- View all ----

    Hidden while the desktop layout is a carousel, and hidden in the same breath
    in the schema. A carousel already *is* the way through the rest of the blog:
    a customer who wants the fourth article drags to it. A button underneath
    saying "view all" alongside a control that already shows all of them is two
    answers to one question, and the second one leaves the page.

    The setting is checked as well as the layout so that turning the row back
    into a grid restores whatever the merchant had chosen, rather than silently
    coming back on.
  endcomment
  assign show_view_all = false
  if s.show_view_all and cs_layout != 'carousel' and featured.articles_count > limit
    assign show_view_all = true
  endif

  comment
    ---- The empty state ----

    A row with no articles is drawn as placeholder cards rather than as a line
    of apologetic text. In the theme editor that is the difference between a
    merchant seeing what the section will look like and a merchant seeing a
    sentence, and it is where the section is judged: **Featured blog** is added
    before the first post is written more often than after.

    How many is derived rather than asked for. One full row is the useful
    preview — it shows the column count, the gaps and the card shape, which is
    everything the layout settings do — so the count is the desktop column
    count, held under **Articles to show** for the merchant who has set that
    lower. Sixteen placeholders for sixteen articles that do not exist is not a
    preview of anything, and a slider for the number of fake cards is a setting
    that stops meaning something the moment the store has posts.
  endcomment
  assign has_articles = false
  if featured.articles.size > 0
    assign has_articles = true
  endif

  assign placeholder_count = desktop
  if placeholder_count > limit
    assign placeholder_count = limit
  endif
-%}

{%- capture section_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', section: s, declarations: true -%}
  --featured-blog-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --featured-blog-margin-block-start: {{ margin_top }}px;
  --featured-blog-margin-block-end: {{ margin_bottom }}px;
  {%- if border_width > 0 -%}
    --featured-blog-border-width: {{ border_width }}px;
    --featured-blog-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="featured-blog color-scheme-container color-{{ s.color_scheme }}{% if has_background_media %} has-background-media{% endif %}"
  data-section-spacing
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  style="{{ section_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
>
  {%- if has_background_media -%}
    {% render 'background-media', settings: s %}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="{% render 'container', width: s.container_width %}">
    {%- comment -%}
      The merchant's own heading cluster. Whatever they add — a Section header,
      a Text block, a row with a button in it — sits above the cards, and this
      section says nothing about what it should be.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <motion-effect
      class="featured-blog__header featured-blog__header--{{ s.alignment | default: 'start' }}"
      {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'text', section: s, children: true %}
    >
      {% content_for 'blocks' %}
    </motion-effect>

    {%- if has_articles -%}
      <swiper-carousel
        {% render 'carousel-shell-attrs',
           settings: s,
           layout: cs_layout,
           layout_mobile: cs_layout_mobile,
           classes: 'featured-blog__carousel',
           columns_desktop: s.columns_desktop,
           columns_tablet: s.columns_tablet,
           columns_mobile: s.columns_mobile,
           count: cs_count %}
      >
        <ul
          class="carousel-shell__track article-grid"
          data-ref="track"
          role="list"
          {% if cs_is_carousel %}aria-label="{{ featured.title | escape }}"{% endif %}
        >
          {%- for article in featured.articles limit: limit -%}
            <li class="article-grid__item carousel-shell__item" data-article-id="{{ article.id }}">
              {% content_for 'block',
                 type: '_article-card',
                 id: 'article-card',
                 closest.article: article,
                 index: forloop.index0,
                 priority: forloop.first,
                 sizes: card_sizes %}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>

        {% render 'carousel-shell-tail',
           settings: s,
           layout: cs_layout,
           layout_mobile: cs_layout_mobile %}
      </swiper-carousel>

      {%- if show_view_all -%}
        <div class="featured-blog__footer">
          {% render 'button', label: 'general.actions.view_all', href: featured.url, variant: 'secondary' %}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The empty row is a plain grid, never a carousel. There is nothing to page
        through, and arrows over placeholder cards invite a merchant to drag a
        track that is one screen wide.

        The columns come from the same three settings the real row uses, written
        here rather than by `carousel-shell-attrs`, because this element is not a
        carousel and should not carry a carousel's attributes.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul
        class="article-grid featured-blog__placeholders"
        role="list"
        style="--columns-desktop: {{ desktop }}; --columns-tablet: {{ s.columns_tablet | default: 2 }}; --columns-mobile: {{ s.columns_mobile | default: 1 }};"
      >
        {%- for i in (1..placeholder_count) -%}
          <li class="article-grid__item">
            {% render 'article-card-placeholder',
               index: forloop.index0,
               sizes: card_sizes,
               section: s %}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.featured_blog.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "@theme"
    },
    {
      "type": "@app"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "blog",
      "id": "blog",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_blog.settings.blog.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "articles_to_show",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_blog.settings.articles_to_show.label",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 16,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_blog.settings.alignment.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "start"
    },

    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.featured_blog.headers.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.layout.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "grid",
          "label": "t:sections.featured_collection.settings.layout.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "carousel",
          "label": "t:sections.featured_collection.settings.layout.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "carousel"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.layout_mobile.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "grid",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.layout.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "carousel",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.layout.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "carousel"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_desktop",
      "label": "t:shared.columns.desktop.label",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_tablet",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.columns_tablet.label",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 4,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.columns_mobile.label",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 3,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "container_width",
      "label": "t:shared.container.width.label",
      "info": "t:shared.container.width.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "edge",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "wide",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "standard",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "compact",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__4.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "custom",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__5.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_view_all",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_collection.settings.show_view_all.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_blog.settings.show_view_all.info",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout != 'carousel' }}"
    },

    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.appearance.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:shared.color_scheme.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "background_media",
      "label": "t:shared.background.media.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "image",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_background",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:shared.background.color.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.color.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_position",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_position.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "cover",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fit",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "cover",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },

    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.borders"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_style.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.options.none"
        },
        {
          "value": "solid",
          "label": "t:shared.options.solid"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_width.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.border_style == 'solid' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_opacity",
      "label": "t:shared.border.opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.border_style == 'solid' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_color.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.border_style == 'solid' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_radius.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },

    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.featured_blog.headers.carousel",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.featured_blog.paragraphs.carousel",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "carousel_speed",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.speed.label",
      "info": "t:shared.carousel.speed.info",
      "min": 100,
      "max": 1500,
      "step": 50,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 500,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "carousel_loop",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.loop.label",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "carousel_autoplay",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.autoplay.label",
      "info": "t:shared.carousel.autoplay.info",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "carousel_autoplay_delay",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.autoplay_delay.label",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 15,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "s",
      "default": 5,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.carousel_autoplay and section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },

    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.carousel.headers.peek",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:shared.carousel.paragraphs.peek",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "carousel_peek_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.peek_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:shared.carousel.peek_mobile.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 90,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "carousel_peek_desktop",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.peek_desktop.label",
      "info": "t:shared.carousel.peek_desktop.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 90,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' }}"
    },

    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.carousel.headers.navigation",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "carousel_navigation",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.navigation.label",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "carousel_nav_position",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_position.label",
      "info": "t:shared.carousel.nav_position.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "outside",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "inside",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_position.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "bottom",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_position.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "inline",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_position.options__4.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "outside",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.carousel_navigation and section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.layout_mobile == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "carousel_nav_icon",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_icon.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "chevron",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_icon.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "arrow",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_icon.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "play",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_icon.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "external",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.nav_icon.options__4.label"
        }
